From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:07:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Gray out the stereo 3D options when OpenGL has no stereo
 buffers

In Preferences, 3D View, the "stereo 3D view" checkbox and the eye
separation are disabled when the 3D view cannot get stereo buffers on
this system, with a tooltip that says why. The stored setting is kept:
a setting that is on stays on and is shown checked.

Stereo3dView::isAvailable() finds out once per session, when the
Preferences window is first shown. With the stereo setting on, the 3D
view's own context format answers it. Otherwise a context is created
with the view's format plus StereoBuffers, without a surface, and its
format is read: Qt picks the framebuffer configuration when it creates
the context (GLX_STEREO on xcb; Qt's EGL contexts are never stereo),
and QOpenGLWidget draws each eye only when its own context's format is
stereo, so this is the same answer the view gets. The context is
created in QGLView2.cc, next to getGLContext() and setGLContext(),
because <QOpenGLContext> does not go together with GLEW.

With Qt before 6.5, where Stereo3dView is a stub, the options are
disabled with their own tooltip.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
(cherry picked from commit c810a549d520b52c6586c78b979b7f7d439d94ba)
